//! The Swage wire contract, defined once and projected everywhere.
//!
//! Anything that crosses a process boundary belongs here as plain serde
//! types. Consumers are derived projections: Rust clients depend on this
//! crate directly, the frontend's TypeScript is generated from it (ts-rs),
//! and the canonical published artifact is the JSON Schema (schemars),
//! committed under `schema/` and regenerated by this crate's tests.
//!
//! The crate is organised into client, hosting, device, and channel surfaces.
//! Each surface emits its own schema document so subset clients can consume
//! only the contract they speak.

pub mod channel;
pub mod client;
pub mod device;
pub mod hosting;
